menuconfig ATM_GFP_DIS
    bool "Device Information Service (DIS) of Google Fast Pair"
    depends on BT && !BT_DIS

    help
	Device Information Service (DIS) of Google Fast Pair
	To prevent tracking access to the Firmware Revision characteristic should be restricted.
	Seeker only allow to read after provisioned. If an attempt is made to read the firmware
	revision, and the Provider isn't bonded nor an authenticated operation was successfully
	completed over that same connection, the Provider should return an unauthenticated error.


if ATM_GFP_DIS

module = ATM_GFP_DIS
module-str = gfp_dis
source "${ZEPHYR_BASE}/subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

config GFP_DIS_FW_VERSION_STR_MAX
    int "Maximum firmware version string length"
    default 100
    range 2 512
    help
	Maximum length of the firmware version string buffer in the Device Information
	Service (DIS). The Google Fast Pair specification does not explicitly limit the
	firmware version string length or mandate a specific format, so this is a
	configurable implementation parameter.

	The buffer must be large enough to accommodate:
	- The firmware version string itself (application-defined format)
	- A null terminator (1 byte)

	Minimum: 2 bytes (allows single character + null terminator)
	Default: 100 bytes (provides reasonable headroom for various version formats)
	Maximum: 512 bytes (practical limit for embedded devices)

	If gfp_dis_init() receives a string longer than this value minus 1 (for null
	terminator), it will reject the string with -ENAMETOOLONG error.

endif # ATM_GFP_DIS
